ARCS Bios should show you (on bottom off screen when in BIOS) what
partitions are available and what the correct ARCS bios name for them is. I
have a small MSDOS partition on an *IDE* harddrive where I boot ldmilo from
and Ive set up an "Enviromental variable set" (it appears as a boot option
on startup) in the bios to boot from:

SystemPartition= scsi(1)disk(0)rdisk(0)partition(1)\
OsLoadPartition= scsi(1)disk(0)rdisk(0)partition(1)\
OsLoader= scsi(1)disk(0)rdisk(0)partition(1)\ldmilo.exe

The motherboard manual and several web pages document more options.

Considering you need floppies to install Linux anyway, why not just put a
floppy drive on the machine? Why go for such an old disty too?



Matt




