Antti J�rvinen wrote:
> 

> Another question is that what is the size of memory bank measured in
> SIMM slots? I've got one memory module where 3/4 of the SIMM slots are
> empty -> how many do I need to fill to add one more bank and do the
> SIMMs need to be similar on whole memory module or only within memory bank?

You'll find that bank is the discrete parity/ECC bank, one SIMM to match
a bank of 4 equally sized SIMMs. Most servers generally, somewhere have
a diagram of how it is laid out.

e.g.

BANK 0 (4 SIMMs) --> PARITY SLOT 0 (total 5 SIMMs)
BANK 1 (4 SIMMs) --> PARITY SLOT 1 (total 5 SIMMs)

etc.

It should NOT be illegal to have different sizes between the banks, but
you cannot mix and match inside the banks. The exception to this if
you're trying to Galaxy inside a multi CPU system, it's memory sensitive
and the LP_*'s at console (variables) need to work on equal physical
boundaries.

-- 
